          "tz": 60
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Etienne AUJAMES",
          "email": "etienne.aujames@cea.fr",
          "date": "2026-11-10 16:10:59.000000000",
          "tz": 60
        },
        "subject": "LU-21175 build: fix specfile with doca 3.2",
        "message": "LU-21175 build: fix specfile with doca 3.2\n\nrpmbuild failed to build lustre with doca 3.2:\n\n```\n$ rpmbuild -ba --with=mofed SPECS/lustre.spec\n...\n++ find -H /usr/src/ofa_kernel/ -type d -name ofed_scripts\n++ xargs dirname\ndirname: missing operand\nTry 'dirname --help' for more information.\n+ o2ib_path=\nerror: Bad exit status from /var/tmp/rpm-tmp.PbAd2W (%build)\n\nRPM build errors:\n    Bad exit status from /var/tmp/rpm-tmp.PbAd2W (%build)\n```\n\nDoca relies on dkms for building and uses symbolic links to point to\nthe build directories in ofa_kernel/default and\nofa_kernel/x86/<kernel>. As a result, find -H returns nothing under\n/usr/src/ofa_kernel.\n\nLook for the OFED devel directory (one containing Module.symvers)\nunder %{mofed_default_path}, in this order:\n 1. the path itself, when --with-o2ib=<path> was passed:\n    e.g: ~/mofed_build/ofa_kernel\n 2. the exact kernel being built:\n    e.g: /usr/src/ofa_kernel/x86_64/6.12.0-211.66.1.el10_2.x86_64\n 3. the default directory (alternatives(8) symlink):\n    e.g: /usr/src/ofa_kernel/default\n 4. the remaining per-kernel directories, newest version first:\n    e.g: /usr/src/ofa_kernel/x86_64/6.12.0-211.66.1.el10_2.x86_64\n         /usr/src/ofa_kernel/x86_64/6.12.0-211.52.1.el10_2.x86_64\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 004af719b2 (\"LU-17507 build: Allow symlink in mofed default path\")\nSigned-off-by: Etienne AUJAMES <eaujames@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: Id2e9ea6576c61fc4b2e24c49ee0110d9fe591c08\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
